# {{NAME_TITLE}} — Failure attribution

Append-only log of what *didn't* work, with the **explicit why**. Reflexion
(Shinn 2023) finding: failure attribution moves the needle more than success
summaries. Most agents skip this — don't.

**Format per entry:**

```markdown
## <slug-of-what-failed>
\`\`\`yaml
importance: 1-10
captured: YYYY-MM-DD
tags: [tag1, tag2]
attribution: behavior | knowledge | timing | tooling | other
\`\`\`

**What I tried:** <one or two sentences>

**Why it failed:** <the actual cause — not "didn't work" but "user wasn't
ready for X because Y", "the tool returned partial data so I drew wrong
conclusion", "rushed past the values question and lost trust">

**What to do differently:** <one concrete adjustment>
```

The dream pass keeps high-importance failures forever and demotes/drops
low-importance ones. Repeated failures of the same `attribution` category
get promoted to `_shared/` as a pattern.

